IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgf-s216b`

-- Tests for sgf-s216b.l4 (s 216B, evidence of shareholders' approval not decisive; Court approval to discontinue).
-- Every expected value below was written from the text of s 216B (src:21859-21884 of CoA1967.txt) before the module was run,
-- never copied from its output. A failing assertion is a finding. Each rule is tried on both sides of each of its conditions.

§ `s 216B(1): the members' approval is not decisive`

-- Arguments: the proceeding is under s 216A; the only reason for the stay or dismissal is the members' approval of the alleged breach.
#ASSERT `s 216B(1) the stay or dismissal is barred where the only reason is the members' approval of the alleged breach` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The stay or dismissal also rests on another reason: outside "by reason only"; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216B(1) the stay or dismissal is barred where the only reason is the members' approval of the alleged breach` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a proceeding under section 216A: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216B(1) the stay or dismissal is barred where the only reason is the members' approval of the alleged breach` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216B(1) the stay or dismissal is barred where the only reason is the members' approval of the alleged breach` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: there is evidence of approval by the members; the Court is making an order under s 216A.
#ASSERT `s 216B(1) the Court may take evidence of approval by the members into account in making an order under section 216A` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216B(1) the Court may take evidence of approval by the members into account in making an order under section 216A` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216B(1) the Court may take evidence of approval by the members into account in making an order under section 216A` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 216B(2): Court approval of a stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal`

-- Arguments: the proceeding is under s 216A; what is sought; the Court has approved it.
-- Each of the four things the subsection lists, without the Court's approval: barred.
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` TRUE `s 216B(2) a stay` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` TRUE `s 216B(2) a discontinuance` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` TRUE `s 216B(2) a settlement` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` TRUE `s 216B(2) a dismissal for want of prosecution` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- With the Court's approval: outside the limit the prohibition sets for itself; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` TRUE `s 216B(2) a settlement` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` TRUE `s 216B(2) a stay` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A dismissal for a reason other than want of prosecution: not in the subsection's list; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` TRUE `s 216B(2) a dismissal for another reason` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not a proceeding under section 216A: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the stay, discontinuance, settlement or dismissal for want of prosecution is barred without the approval of the Court` FALSE `s 216B(2) a stay` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: the proceeding is under s 216A; the Court is giving its approval.
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the Court may give its approval upon such terms as it thinks fit` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the Court may give its approval upon such terms as it thinks fit` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the Court may give its approval upon such terms as it thinks fit` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: the proceeding is under s 216A; the Court has determined that a complainant's interest may be substantially affected.
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the Court may order a party to give notice to the complainant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The "if" gate (the Court's determination) is not met: the grant is not made out; not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the Court may order a party to give notice to the complainant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 216B(2) the Court may order a party to give notice to the complainant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 216B(3): interim costs`

#ASSERT `s 216B(3) the Court may order the company to pay the complainant interim costs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216B(3) the Court may order the company to pay the complainant interim costs` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "Including legal fees and disbursements": a listed item holds; anything else is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 216B(3) the interim costs the Court may order include the item` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 216B(3) the interim costs the Court may order include the item` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments: the Court has ordered the company to pay the complainant interim costs; the application or action has been finally disposed of.
#ASSERT `s 216B(3) the complainant may be accountable for the interim costs` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not yet finally disposed of: the "upon" gate fails (split site (ii): JUST FALSE by the delegated-definitions ruling, item (c); the other reading is NOTHING).
#ASSERT `s 216B(3) the complainant may be accountable for the interim costs` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- No interim costs were ordered: nothing to account for.
#ASSERT `s 216B(3) the complainant may be accountable for the interim costs` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 216B(3) the complainant may be accountable for the interim costs` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
